## Ignore Visual Studio temporary files, build results, and
## files generated by popular Visual Studio add-ons.
##
## This .gitignore file is a combination of several sources:
## 1. The official Microsoft Visual Studio .gitignore file:
##    https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/master/VisualStudio.gitignore
## 2. Common entries for C# and .NET projects.

# Build results
[Dd]ebug/
[Dd]ebugPublic/
[Rr]elease/
[Rr]eleases/
x64/
x86/
[Ww][33][22]/
[Aa][Rr][Mm]/
[Aa][Rr][Mm]64/
bld/
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
[Ll]og/
[Ll]ogs/

# Visual Studio 2015/2017/2019/2022 cache and settings
.vs/
# Uncomment if you want to ignore the whole .vs folder
# .vs/

# User-specific files
*.rsuser
*.suo
*.user
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates

# Visual Studio Code design-time settings
.vscode/

# User-specific files (DotSettings)
*.DotSettings.user

# Roslyn cache directories
*.ide/

# NuGet Packages
*.nupkg
# NuGet Symbol Packages
*.snupkg
# The packages folder can be ignored because of Package Restore
**/[Pp]ackages/*
# except build/, which is used as an MSBuild target.
!**/[Pp]ackages/build/
# Uncomment if using NuGet repositories to store project specific packages (not recommended)
# !**/[Pp]ackages/

# Microsoft Azure Build Output
csx/
*.pubxml
*.azurePubxml

# Others
sql/
*.Cache
ClientBin/
[Ss]tyle[Cc]op.[Cc]ache
~*
*~
*.dbmdl
*.dbproj.user
*.publishsettings
*.swp
*.bak
*.log
*.patch
*.diff

# JetBrains Rider
.idea/
*.sln.iml

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.tmp.driveupload/
*.docx
*.pptx
